  "published": "2026-07-31T02:34:35.14Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v4.0.0-alpha.10: hotfix. RegisterAsync opened its own transaction OUTSIDE the context execution strategy, so every consumer configuring EnableRetryOnFailure (the standard setup against Azure SQL) failed on EVERY user registration -- public and administrative -- with \"The configured execution strategy does not support user-initiated transactions\". The transaction now runs inside Database.CreateExecutionStrategy().ExecuteAsync(...). No API change and no configuration change: consumers only need to upgrade. The bug survived because the suite runs on the InMemory provider, whose default strategy does not retry and therefore never trips EF guard; the regression test added with the fix runs on Sqlite with a retrying strategy. See UPGRADE.md 23. API may still change before stable.",
